From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: André Braga <code@andrebraga.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: flush the crash state free after the GPU worker stops

Draining the GPU worker can still capture a crash state, so flush the
deferred free after kthread_destroy_worker() and release a registered
devcoredump before it, as the author agreed in review:
CAJZkD00oU9iCm4J6EM_yJ7NwjRwABudzTsa9wN23hmTTLWo7nw@mail.gmail.com.
Drop once the author's v2 lands.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -1062,10 +1062,6 @@
 
 	DBG("%s", gpu->name);
 
-	/* May be unset if probe failed before msm_gpu_init() */
-	if (gpu->crashstate_free_work.func)
-		flush_work(&gpu->crashstate_free_work);
-
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(gpu->rb); i++) {
 		msm_ringbuffer_destroy(gpu->rb[i]);
 		gpu->rb[i] = NULL;
@@ -1083,6 +1079,17 @@
 		kthread_destroy_worker(gpu->worker);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Nothing captures a crash state any more: release a devcoredump that
+	 * is still registered and wait for the free it, or a drained
+	 * recover_work, queued. May be unset if probe failed before
+	 * msm_gpu_init().
+	 */
+	if (gpu->crashstate_free_work.func) {
+		dev_coredump_put(&gpu->pdev->dev);
+		flush_work(&gpu->crashstate_free_work);
+	}
+
 	msm_devfreq_cleanup(gpu);
 	msm_perfcntr_cleanup(gpu);
 
